settings.txt layout:
-port number
-turn timeout in seconds
-maximum lobby size
-maximum time to wait once there are 2 players (specify 0 for unlimited wait time)
-api endpoint to report games to (currently unused)
-api key for the above endpoint (currently unused)
-card names, where a blank line separates categories

Server protocol quick reference:
-TCP port 0xC10E (49422) by default.
-Data from the server comes in continuous frames with the following layout:
+-----------------------------------------------+
| 1 byte     | 3 bytes  | 4 bytes     | X bytes |
| FRAME TYPE | RESERVED | DATA LENGTH | DATA    |
+-----------------------------------------------+
-Data sent to the server should have the same format.
-Integers will never use the sign bit so they can be treated as signed or unsigned.
-0xFF... (-1) may be used to indicate an invalid value where 0 would not be appropriate.
-All integers are big endian.
-The category can be predicted by the card ID. If there are 7 cards in category 0, card ID 6 belongs to category 0, and card ID 7 belongs to category 1.